call_indirect`), start, globals, custom `name`/`producers` | gap (D16 prompt theme; unasked) | import section id 2 (`env.*`/`wasi_snapshot_preview1.*`), table id 4, elem id 9, `call_indirect` 0x11 | [I] `wasm-objdump -x -j Import -j Export -j Table -j Elem f`; extend `lib.binary.wasm_layout` | med-high (theme ids could land with tomorrow's carry-over backfill) |\n| 68 | WASM from real toolchains (Emscripten, wasi-sdk/clang, Rust, Go, AssemblyScript), memory64, passive segments, HCFG in custom section / split / i32.store-built | gap | `global.get __memory_base` init expr, `memory.init` 0xfc 08, `producers` section, AssemblyScript UTF-16 strings, Go `go:buildid` | [I] `wasm2wat`, `wasm-decompile`; `hcfg_scan` (utf16) ; clang-18 `--target=wasm32-wasi -c` (object only: no wasm-ld) | med |\n| 69 | eBPF object (ELF e_machine 247) | gap | ELF64 ET_REL, sections `license`, `.maps`, `xdp`/`kprobe/...`/`tracepoint/...`, `.BTF`/`.BTF.ext` | [I] `readelf -hSW f.o` (machine \"Linux BPF\"); `llvm-objdump-18 -d f.o`; `clang-18 -target bpf -c` builds fixtures | med (natural \"sandboxed code\" sequel to WASM) |\n| 70 | Bytecode containers: LLVM bitcode, Python `.pyc`, Lua `luac`, standalone `.class`/`.dex` | gap | `BC\\xc0\\xde` / wrapper `de c0 17 0b`; pyc magic `xx 0d 0d 0a`; `\\x1bLua`; `CAFEBABE` major>=45; `dex\\n035` | [I] `llvm-dis-18`/`llvm-bcanalyzer-18`; `pycdas`; `luac -l -l`; `javap`; jadx | low-med (format label unknown -> submit alone) |\n| 71 | Section-less / corrupted ELF headers (sstrip, e_shnum 0, bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx) | gap | `readelf -S`: \"There are no sections\", pyelftools exceptions, PT_LOAD only | [I] `readelf -lW f`; parse program headers; `rz-bin -I f`; HCFG via raw scan | med (next escalation of \"Stripped\") |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nSTEP 1  file -b F ; xxd -l 64 F            -> container + arch + stripped/static/PIE in one line\n  7f454c46 ELF: byte4 1=ELF32 2=ELF64; byte5 1=LE 2=BE (BE => read e_machine/HCFG ints big-endian)\n  4d5a MZ->PE: Machine 0x14c i386 | 0x8664 x86-64 | 0xaa64 AArch64 | 0x1c0/0x1c4 ARM; \"Mono/.Net\" => pe_cli\n  cffaedfe/cefaedfe Mach-O thin; cafebabe + small u32 nfat => Mach-O FAT (NOT a Java class) ; format word presumed `macho`\n  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n  0061736d \\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32` (GM-confirmed); lib.binary.wasm_layout -> sections, memories,\n    data_segments (file_offset + mem_offset); wasm-objdump -x F ; HCFG RAW in data seg 0 -> raw scan finds it (crc-gate)\n  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\nSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  NOT FOUND => blob is hidden: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / overlay past last section;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (D15 stripped/symbolized, D16 compact/direct;\n  match the LONGEST member-name token, a tag may contain `_`) ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"build-pair-router\", \"concept\": \"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs dynamic, -pie vs -no-pie, -g vs stripped, upx'd vs plain, each with a `.hcfg` section and file-name tags. Target: router matches the LONGEST tag token of exactly one member name; structural fallback per tag family (no INTERP = static, ET_DYN+INTERP = pie, UPX! = packed, .debug_info = debug, smaller code = compact/optimized); per-member fields that DIFFER inside a pair (elf_type, entry_point, has_symtab, section_names, imports) answered from that member; sha256_K from zip central-directory order.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cross-arch-pair\", \"concept\": \"Same source built for x86-64 + AArch64 (+ RISC-V/ARM .o) as a pair, arch-named qualifiers\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15 links, clang-18 --target=riscv64/armv7 -c gives ET_REL. Name tags like `-x86_64.elf`/`-aarch64.elf`/`-arm64` put an UNDERSCORE inside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_64_machine`): the router must try multi-token tags before splitting at the first `_`. Expected labels from multiarch-machine-labels (x86-64, AArch64, RISC-V, ARM; kind:integer 62/183/243/40); HCFG ints stay LE on these arches.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-inventory-fields\", \"concept\": \"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add them. Build fixtures with wat2wasm (installed): imports from env/wasi_snapshot_preview1 (func/memory/table/global), funcref table + active elem, call_indirect, start, mutable globals, passive segment, name + producers custom sections. Extend lib.binary.wasm_layout with imports [{module,name,kind}], exports [{name,kind,index}], tables, elems, start, globals, custom_names; candidate spellings: JSON list of `module.name` in section order, counts as integers, memory_min in pages, has_table true/false, hcfg_offset = file offset of the `H` (record mem_offset too).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\", \"concept\": \"WASM HCFG