": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets: parser never crashes (pyelftools wrapped, header fields from raw struct), section_names `[]`, has_symtab false, has_hcfg_section false unless the literal name exists, HCFG via raw scan; entry_point/machine still from the ELF header.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as int and ISO. Fixtures from the existing TARGETS.json builds (gcc -g, -Wl,--build-id). Spellings unknown -> submit alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions (`dll!func`?), exports, imphash; Mach-O LC_LOAD_DYLIB. JSON compact like symbols. D15 symbolized had getenv/strcmp/printf, unasked.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign-arch ELF decoders (ARM/AArch64/MIPS/PPC/RISC-V)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install qemu-user-static binfmt-support (only qemu-system-* are installed now). Use only inside the bwrap sandbox, never on the host; static analysis remains the default.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"Haskell, OCaml, Fortran, Ada, V, Odin, COBOL, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-singlefile-aot\", \"concept\": \".NET single-file bundle, ReadyToRun and NativeAOT builds\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"dotnet installed: `dotnet publish -p:PublishSingleFile=true` (apphost + bundle manifest, `.net core bundle` signature hash), `-p:PublishReadyToRun=true` (R2R header in CLI dll), `-p:PublishAot=true` (native ELF, no BSJB). Targets: format label shift (pe_cli vs elf), HCFG location inside the bundle (embedded dll offset) -> hcfg_scan on the bundle bytes.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upx-packed-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"UPX-packed ELF/PE (plain and with scrubbed UPX! magic / renamed sections)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: `upx -9` a C ELF + MinGW PE carrying an HCFG `.hcfg` section; variant with `UPX!` zeroed and UPX0/1 renamed. Target: solver detects (packer_info), restores magic, `upx -d` on a copy, then hcfg_find + header fields of the UNPACKED image; record which bytes (packed vs unpacked) sha256/format/has_hcfg_section are answered from. upx 4.2.4 installed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"aes-tea-chacha-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG encrypted with AES-128/256 (ECB/CBC/CTR), XTEA, ChaCha20\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture style of TARGETS.json: key/IV as adjacent 16/32-byte raw or printable strings, or derived (sha256 of campaign-like string). Extractor: locate cipher by constants (S-box 637c777b, 0x9e3779b9, 'expand 32-byte k'), try candidate keys within +-4 KB, accept when plaintext starts 'HCFG' and crc-gates. pycryptodome installed.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stack-built-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG assembled at runtime from mov-immediate stores / per-char pushes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: gcc -O0/-O2 C that writes the blob via volatile stack stores (x86-64 and AArch64). Extractor: capstone imm collection per function in store order, fallback unicorn emulation of the builder (no syscalls), then hcfg_find on the buffer. Offset convention unknown: record the first mov instruction's file offset as a speculative guess.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"multiarch-machine-labels\", \"concept\": \"ELF/PE/Mach-O machine words for i386, ARM, AArch64, MIPS(el), PPC/PPC64, RISC-V, SPARC + big-endian HCFG ints\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib/knowledge.py ELF_MACHINE has only 4 entries. Fixtures: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc (linkable) and clang-18 --target=<arch> -c (ET_REL .o; no lld installed) each with a `.hcfg` section, LE and BE. Expected labels = readelf spelling (x86, ARM, AArch64, MIPS R3000, PowerPC, PowerPC64, RISC-V, Sparc v9) with decimal e_machine for kind:integer; check hcfg_scan handles BE u16/u32 header fields.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"macho-hcfg-section\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O thin + fat universal binary with HCFG in a `__DATA,__hcfg` section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"clang-18 --target=x86_64-apple-macos -c and arm64-apple-macos -c produce MH_OBJECT files (no ld64); hand-pack a FAT header with python for the universal case. Targets: format label (`macho` presumed), machine from cputype (0x01000007 -> x86-64, 0x0100000c -> AArch64), has_hcfg_section on segment,section names, fat-vs-Java cafebabe disambiguation, lib.binary.macho_facts over both slices.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"resource-overlay-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"HCFG in PE RT_RCDATA, .NET manifest resource, jar non-class entry, or file overlay\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: MinGW-free path = patch a resource dir with pefile into a small PE; dnfile resource in a dotnet-built dll; jar with config.bin; ELF/PE with blob appended past the last section. Confirm hcfg_scan finds each and record offset convention (resource data start vs magic) plus a speculative has_overlay/overlay_offset.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"rolling-xor-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"Index-dependent xor (key+i, key^prev, xor with len/crc)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend the bytemap/mxor fixture family: known-plaintext 'HCFG' recovers the start key and step; brute 256 x {add,sub,xor-prev} modes, crc-gate. Not covered by current single-byte or repeating-key xor.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"init-time-decoder\", \"concept\": \"Config decoded in .init_array constructor / TLS callback / DllMain\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture with __attribute__((constructor)) decoding a stored blob; extractor finds .init_array targets and emulates them with unicorn (stdlib-free). Low until a day theme hints at runtime behaviour.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"shared-object-relocatable\", \"concept\": \"ET_DYN .so / ET_REL .o / DLL members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"gcc -shared and gcc -c fixtures with .hcfg; expected elf_type ET_DYN/ET_REL, entry_point 0x0 for .o, exported-symbol config. PE DLL via objdump -p export table.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"exotic-codecs\", \"concept\": \"base58/base62/base91/z85 and lz4/zstd/brotli HCFG\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"tools/pybase62 + tools/pybase91 + python lz4 exist; pip install zstandard brotli into the venv. Add hcfg_fixtures entries with speculative offset = first stored byte.\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e009bdf-b1d9-40f4-ba0d-457d0a7abfa4","uuid":"35dacbe9-5c58-4c74-b474-d2c6c2f8c711","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:10:50.678Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| 48 | Multibyte xor / byte maps (nibble-swap, NOT, add/sub, rol) | prebuilt multibyte-xor, nibble-swap-bitnot | no magic; high-ish entropy