{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UYkMAh9s4xot96w1H8tyVQ","type":"tool_result","content":"8\tProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\n9\tlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix taken from the file-name tag (D15 C ELF\n10\t`stripped`/`symbolized`; D16 WebAssembly `compact`/`direct` = two codegens of one function, first non-native container since the\n11\tjars: labels `wasm`/`wasm32`, HCFG RAW in active data segment 0). Expect the pair axis to continue (static/dynamic, O0/O2,\n12\tPIE/no-PIE, packed/unpacked, x86-64/AArch64) and more non-ELF containers (Mach-O, eBPF, bytecode). Asked field names are a small\n13\tfixed pool (config_*, format, machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names,\n14\tdisassembly, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, xor_key_hex, metadata_version,\n15\tcompression_methods); the prompt's language theme has not been asked since D4. So for D17+ the biggest risks are (a) a twist that\n16\thides the HCFG from a byte scan (packing, real crypto, stack-built), (b) a new container/arch whose LABEL we have never spelled\n17\t(Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64, MIPS...), (c) a new field family (imports/exports, memory/table \"doors\" -- the D16 prompt's theme --,\n18\tbuild-id, protections), (d) a pair qualifier that itself contains `_` (`x86_64_machine`) breaking a split-at-first-`_` router.\n19\t\n20\tTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n21\tInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\n22\tllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\n23\trizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\n24\tAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\n25\tjadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n26\t7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\n27\tlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e009bdf-b1d9-40f4-ba0d-457d0a7abfa4","uuid":"79d77814-aef0-4f02-9d00-1df06706083c","timestamp":"2026-10-17T13:13:58.129Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"Progression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix taken from the file-name tag (D15 C ELF\n`stripped`/`symbolized`; D16 WebAssembly `compact`/`direct` = two codegens of one function, first non-native container since the\njars: labels `wasm`/`wasm32`, HCFG RAW in active data segment 0). Expect the pair axis to continue (static/dynamic, O0/O2,\nPIE/no-PIE, packed/unpacked, x86-64/AArch64) and more non-ELF containers (Mach-O, eBPF, bytecode). Asked field names are a small\nfixed pool (config_*, format, machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names,\ndisassembly, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, xor_key_hex, metadata_version,\ncompression_methods); the prompt's language theme has not been asked since D4. So for D17+ the biggest risks are (a) a twist that\nhides the HCFG from a byte scan (packing, real crypto, stack-built), (b) a new container/arch whose LABEL we have never spelled\n(Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64, MIPS...), (c) a new field family (imports/exports, memory/table \"doors\" -- the D16 prompt's theme --,\nbuild-id, protections), (d) a pair qualifier that itself contains `_` (`x86_64_machine`) breaking a split-at-first-`_` router.\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).","numLines":20,"startLine":8,"totalLines":175}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UYkMAh9s4xot96w1H8tyVQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
