b) the new-day member keeps being a\nplain ELF whose ids the carried-over solver already answers (D17 group banked at T+18 s); (c) label fields with no derivable\nspelling (`hcfg_storage` raw, D3 `pe_cli`) are the real time sink. Asked field names: config_*, format, machine, architecture,\nelf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols, section_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*,\nhas_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags,\nmethod_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset, hcfg_version, hcfg_storage, xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods.\nRemaining risks: (1) more per-language fact backfills, (2) a twist that hides the HCFG from a byte scan (the D17 \"decoder\" theme\ndid not materialise but stays plausible: packing, real crypto, stack-built, per-string encryption, API hashing), (3) a new\ncontainer/arch label (Mach-O, eBPF, AArch64...), (4) more pair days with `_`-containing tags.\n\n'''\ns = s[:start] + prog + s[end:]\n\n# 3. concept table\ns = s.replace('| standard tool + exact command | D16+ likelihood |', '| standard tool + exact command | D18+ likelihood |')\nlines = s.split('\\n')\nfor i, l in enumerate(lines):\n    if l.startswith('| 18 | Ada (GNAT) |'):\n        lines[i] = ('| 18 | Ada (GNAT) | **seen D17** (1.4 MB dynamic ELF, GNAT 14.2.0, not stripped, DWARF) | `GNAT Version: 14.2.0`, `ada__*`/`system__*`/'\n                    '`__gnat_*` symbols, `ADA.STRINGS.*_ERROR`, `.gcc_except_table`; HCFG RAW in `.rodata` | [I] `strings -a f \\\\| grep -m1 \\'GNAT Version\\'`; '\n                    '`grep -abo HCFG f` (crc-gate); Ada names `pkg__sub` -> `pkg.sub`; [M] gnat (no fixture builds) | high (carry-over; '\n                    'a backfill may ask `has_gnat_runtime`/decoder facts) |')\n    if l.startswith('| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) |'):\n        lines[i] = l.replace('seen D1, D15 (+ every day\\'s d01)', 'seen D1, D15 (+ every day\\'s d01; D17 re-asked marker/recover_code)')\n    if l.startswith('| 7 | Java / Kotlin jar |'):\n        lines[i] = l.replace('seen D6, D7', 'seen D6, D7 (D17 re-asked methods/access_flags/method_count/has_coroutine_runtime)')\n    if l.startswith('| 66 | Same-source build PAIR'):\n        lines[i] = l.replace('| high (2 days running;', '| med-high (D15-D16 pairs, D17 broke the streak; D17 backfill asked config ids for the other tag too;')\n    if l.startswith('| 67 | WASM \"doors\" inventory'):\n        lines[i] = re.sub(r'\\| [^|]*\\|$', '| high (prebuilt wasm-inventory-fields; the D17 backfill pattern = old days\\' themes get asked later on their group) |', l)\n    if l.startswith('| 71 |'):\n        idx = i\nnew_rows = [\n '| 72 | Backfill of an earlier day\\'s single-solve facts on its old group | seen D8 (pad to 10), **D17** (pad to 11: marker, recover_code, '\n 'mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_coroutine_runtime) | '\n 'ids on dNN groups that the solver\\'s field table does not know; generic `field N` wording | [I] per-language facts dict in the solver; '\n '`javap -v -p`, `nm`, `readelf -sW`, `GoReSym` | high (next backfill likely reaches D8-D17 facts: swift5 sections/protocols, Nim/D/Crystal '\n 'runtimes, Zig/FPC/ObjC class+selector lists, pair diffs, wasm exports, Ada GNAT) |',\n '| 73 | `hcfg_storage` label (how the blob is stored) | **seen D17** (exact_text on d08/d09/d11-d14) | base64 `SENGR` literal vs raw `HCFG` | '\n '`base64` GM-confirmed; RAW word UNKNOWN (~117 spellings rejected, list in the technique log) | high (re-asked every backfill day; '\n 'never batch the raw ones) |',\n '| 74 | Config decoder routine as answer (algorithm, key, function name, loop shape) | gap (D17 prompt \"recover the reversible decoder\", unasked) | '\n 'function xrefing the stored blob; `xor byte [..], imm8` / `xor al, 0x73` loops; Ada `pkg__decode_config` | [I] capstone over the function '\n 'referencing the blob VA; `rizin -q -c \\'aaa; axt @ <blob va>\\' f` | med (theme may be backfilled on d17 later) |',\n]\nlines[idx+1:idx+1] = new_rows\ns = '\\n'.join(lines)\n\n# 4. recognition cues (code block)\ns = s.replace(\"STEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\",\n              \"STEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\")\ns = s.replace(\"  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\\n```\",\n \"  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\\n\"\n \"  D17 Ada ELF (GNAT 14.2): plain ELF, HCFG RAW in .rodata -> carried-over solver answers it unchanged.\\n\"\n \"BACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\\n\"\n \"  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\\n\"\n \"  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\\n\"\n \"  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\\n\"\n \"hcfg_storage: base64 literal -> `base64` (GM). RAW -> unknown word: send ALONE, cap ~10 probes, then HELP; never batch it.\\n```\")\n\n# 5. gaps\ngs = s.index('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n') + len('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n')\nge = s.index('\\n```', gs)\ngaps = json.loads(s[gs:ge])\nbyid = {g['id']: g for g in gaps}\nnew = [\n {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_coroutine_runtime). Build ONE generic facts table so the D8-D17 analogues answer without code: has_swift_runtime (swift5_* sections / `$s` symbols), has_nim_runtime (NimMain), has_zig_runtime (.comment zig / `std.` panic strings), has_d_runtime (`_D4core`/`_D2rt`), has_fpc_runtime (FPC banner / `.fpcdata`), has_crystal_runtime (`Crystal:H`/`*crystal*`), has_objc_runtime (`__objc_*` sections, objc_msg_lookup), has_gnat_runtime (`GNAT Version`, `__gnat_`), has_wasm_*; plus name lists: ObjC classes/selectors (`._OBJC_CLASS_`, `objc_sel_name_`), Swift type/protocol names (demangled `$s` nominal types), Nim procs (`<proc>__<mod>_u<N>`), D functions (`_D<len>`), Ada subprograms (`pkg__sub`), mangled forms kept (GM wants MANGLED). Fixtures: the cached real members from day08-day17 single_solve/work/extracted (bytes on disk) + expected values in a table; every field returns `none`/`false` on absence, never raises.\"},\n {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>) of the Main-Class. Next backfill may ask major_version/minor_version, constant_pool_count, super_class, interfaces, field names/count, method descriptors, SourceFile attribute, main_class (Manifest), class_count/entry_count, Kotlin `@Metadata` d1/d2, invokeSuspend label states. Implement a stdlib ClassFile parser in lib (javap -v -p parity tests on fixture jars built with javac/kotlinc-free hand-made classes); JSON compact, table order, decimal ints.\"},\n {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typedef/method names, method_count, assembly_name, assembly_version, target_framework (runtimeconfig tfm), entry_point token hex, has_field_rva. Use dnfile (installed) + ilspycmd parity on a dotnet-built fixture dll; JSON lists in table order, `<Module>` and `<PrivateImplementationDetails>` kept as named.\"},\n {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any HCFG group). From the validated HcfgHit: compute blob VA, find code xrefs (RIP-relative lea/mov to VA in .text via capstone, or rizin `axt`), report the containing FUNC symbol (Ada `pkg__decode_config`, Nim/D/Crystal mangled kept), the xor immediate(s) inside the loop and whether it equals header key; return algorithm token `xor` speculative. Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 C decoders (xor, add, rol, rolling) with symbols and stripped.\"},\n {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, fortran, cobol, odin, v, dart, julia, kotlin-native, python(pyinstaller/nuitka). Cue table = atlas STEP 3 regex + section/symbol markers; verify on every cached dNN member (expected = the day's language), log ambiguity rather than guess.\"},\n {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (installed): map the ELF PT_LOADs, set rsp to a scratch stack, run from the FUNC symbol until ret with an instruction cap, read eax; refuse on syscalls/calls into libc. Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 builds with arithmetic-constant and table-lookup returns; AArch64 via unicorn ARM64 for the cross-arch case.\"},\n {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports resolved by hash (ROR13, djb2, FNV-1a, CRC32, murmur) -> resolved API list / hash algorithm fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"Natural 'encoded' sequel to D17 for a decoder-themed day. Precompute hash tables for libc/kernel32/ntdll export names under the common algorithms; scan .rodata/.text immediates (capstone `cmp`/`mov` imm32) and report matches in code order, algorithm token, seed. Fixtures: small C ELF/MinGW PE resolving getenv/printf by djb2 and ror13.\"},\n {\"id\": \"per-string-encryption\", \"concept\": \"Every string (not just HCFG) encrypted individually with a shared decoder (xor/add per string, stack strings) -> decoded string lists as fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\": \"Escalation of the D17 'encoded configuration' theme: config fields stored as separate xor'd strings instead of one HCFG blob. Use floss (installed in .venv) + a capstone pass collecting (ptr,len,key) triples from decoder call sites; decode all, crc/regex-gate (domains, BRNN-, Global\\\\\\\\). Fixtures: C ELF with 5 xor-encrypted strings + stack strings, -O0/-O2.\"},\n {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-raw-label\", \"concept\": \"GM word for a RAW-stored HCFG in `hcfg_storage` (d12 FPC .data, d14 ObjC .hcfg)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n  \"detail\": \"D17: `base64` confirmed for SENGR literals; ~117 raw spellings rejected (raw, plain, bytes, binary, blob, xor, section, data, .data, .hcfg, rodata, struct, literal, inline, embedded, none, base64 and combos -- full list in the technique log). Untried: hex, encoded, xor_encoded, obfuscated, magic, header, framed, typed_const, array_of_byte, c_array, uint8_array, objc_section, fpc_data. When re-asked: submit raw ids ALONE after everything else banked, cap ~10 probes, then HELP; ask the organizers if a hint channel exists. Never let it hold the other ids.\"},\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g['id'] not in byid, g['id']\n# re-rank existing\nfor gid, p in {\"build-pair-router\": 2, \"cross-arch-pair\": 2, \"wasm-inventory-fields\": 2, \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\": 3,\n               \"native-imports-exports-facts\": 1, \"provenance-facts-extractor\": 1, \"ebpf-object\": 2,\n               \"bytecode-containers\": 3, \"sstrip-corrupt-headers\": 2}.items():\n    byid[gid]['priority'] = p\nbyid['native-imports-exports-facts']['detail'] += ' D17 backfill pattern (old days re-asked as per-group facts) makes imports/NEEDED lists a likely next field on any native group.'\nbyid['provenance-facts-extractor']['detail'] += ' D17 member had DWARF (Ada, producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0`): dwarf_language/producer is a plausible backfill id for d05/d11/d17.'\nnl = byid['new-language-fingerprints']\nnl['concept'] = 'Haskell, OCaml, Fortran, V, Odin, COBOL, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka (Ada seen D17)'\nnl['detail'] = nl['detail'].replace('gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed', 'Ada landed D17 as a plain ELF with RAW HCFG -- the law held. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed')\nout = new[:4] + [byid['native-imports-exports-facts'], byid['provenance-facts-extractor'], new[8]] + new[4:8] + \\\n      [g for g in gaps if g['id'] not in ('native-imports-exports-facts', 'provenance-facts-extractor')]\nout.sort(key=lambda g: g['priority'])  # stable\nfor g in out: assert set(g) == {\"id\",\"concept\",\"priority\",\"action\",\"detail\"}, g['id']\ntxt = '[\\n' + ',\\n'.join('  ' + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in out) + '\\n]'\njson.loads(txt)\ns = s[:gs] + txt + s[ge:]\nopen(F, 'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\nF=reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md; awk '/^## Recognition cues/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f' $F | wc -l; wc -l $F; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json,re\ns=open('reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md').read()\ng=json.loads(s.split('## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n')[1].split('\\n```')[0])\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('binary-reverse-engineering:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), 'pending prebuild:', len(pend), pend)\nprint([ (x['id'],x['priority']) for x in g][:14])\nE","description":"Apply atlas edits and validate gaps"}}}
